name: sim.transformImage
description: Transforms an image in various ways
luaSynopsis: bytes newImage = sim.transformImage(bytes image, list resolution, int options)
pythonSynopsis: buffer newImage = sim.transformImage(buffer image, int[2] resolution, int options)
inputs:
1. image: buffer to rgb or rgba values of the image. Beware that in Lua, this image buffer will be modified!
2. resolution: resolution of the image
3. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): the provided image is rgba (or a depth buffer, i.e. one double per image pixel), otherwise it is rgb
    - bit1 set (2): the image will be flipped on its x-axis
    - bit2 set (4): the image will be flipped on its y-axis
outputs:
1. newImage: buffer of the transformed image
replacedBy:
- name: transformImage, class: app, file: app_transformImage.method
